ctive member of the same space with ADMIN role; a missing actor membership, non-normal actor status where checked, or non-ADMIN role returns the permission-denied error.","object":"different-member removal","evidenceIds":["ev-c94742fb0bfe5a814b0b","ev-3a0594503f4ea8a13255","ev-e0a46c4a3d1b9ca13b49"]},{"questionId":"delete-space-member","kind":"guard","state":"observed","subject":"self-removal guard","claim":"When actorUserID equals the target UserID, the different-member ADMIN check is bypassed in all three examined database implementations. The target still must resolve as an active membership for the delete to affect a row; the source also validates positive identifiers at the store boundary.","object":"self-removal","evidenceIds":["ev-c94742fb0bfe5a814b0b","ev-3a0594503f4ea8a13255","ev-e0a46c4a3d1b9ca13b49","ev-24a4b30e6d9d6dd8562d"]},{"questionId":"delete-space-member","kind":"effect","state":"observed","subject":"membership deletion effect","claim":"After authorization and target checks, each examined backend deletes the active space_member row for the selected space and user and commits the transaction. Thus the protected effect is the selected target membership, not an unrelated object.","object":"active space_member row","evidenceIds":["ev-c94742fb0bfe5a814b0b","ev-3a0594503f4ea8a13255","ev-e0a46c4a3d1b9ca13b49"]},{"questionId":"delete-space-member","kind":"exception","state":"observed","subject":"last-admin exception","claim":"Removal of an active, normal ADMIN is denied when the space has one or fewer active normal ADMINs, returning the last-admin error. This restriction applies to both self-removal and removal by another administrator when the target is the last such admin.","object":"active normal ADMIN membership","evidenceIds":["ev-c94742fb0bfe5a814b0b","ev-3a0594503f4ea8a13255","ev-e0a46c4a3d1b9ca13b49"]},{"questionId":"delete-space-member","kind":"exception","state":"unresolved","subject":"upstream identity and middleware","claim":"The provided source excerpts establish the store's actorUserID checks but do not establish, from a complete API-handler read, how the external caller is bound to actorUserID or whether deployment middleware adds protections. Those facts are not assumed; they are not needed to establish the visible store-level distinction between self-removal and different-member removal.","object":"API/deployment boundary","evidenceIds":["ev-8587192a0a224bab1e1c","ev-8cc3386f0794bfc13e1b","ev-9ee45f98c8803e5baf45","ev-6f0761b3437bb3341438"]}],"questions":[{"questionId":"delete-space-member","behavior":{"disposition":"conditional","explanation":"Actual visible behavior is conditional: self-removal is allowed for a resolvable active membership, subject to the last-active-normal-admin safeguard; removal of a different member is allowed only when the caller is an active ADMIN of that same space, and is denied for an ordinary USER. Therefore an ordinary current member may not remove a different member under the visible enforcement."},"branches":[{"id":"different-ordinary-member","condition":"actorUserID != target UserID and actor is a current active ordinary USER of the same space","disposition":"deny","explanation":"The backend requires the actor's same-space membership role to be ADMIN; a non-ADMIN returns permission denied.","evidenceIds":["ev-c94742fb0bfe5a814b0b","ev-3a0594503f4ea8a13255","ev-e0a46c4a3d1b9ca13b49"]},{"id":"different-admin-member","condition":"actorUserID != target UserID and actor is an active ADMIN of the same space","disposition":"allow","explanation":"The different-member role guard passes. The target must exist as an active member, and removal of the last active normal ADMIN remains denied.","evidenceIds":["ev-c94742fb0bfe5a814b0b","ev-3a0594503f4ea8a13255","ev-e0a46c4a3d1b9ca13b49"]},{"id":"self-removal-nonlast-admin-or-user","condition":"actorUserID == target UserID and the selected membership exists and is not the last active normal ADMIN","disposition":"allow","explanation":"